# Serving-only environment. Copy to api/.env (gitignored).
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS, AND NOT THE REPO-ROOT .env
# ------------------------------------------------
# api/main.py loads BOTH the repo-root .env and this one. The eval flows —
# mlflow/ragflow.py, agentflow.py, retrievalflow.py — load the repo-root .env
# and mlflow/.env, and never this file. So this is the one place where a
# variable reaches the API and cannot reach an eval run.
#
# That matters for exactly one reason, and it is a silent failure:
# MLflow treats a configured OTLP endpoint as EXCLUSIVE. Put
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_TRACES_ENDPOINT in the repo-root .env and an eval run
# picks it up too, ships its trace to the collector instead of to MLflow, and
# DeepEval is left with no retrieval_context and no tools_called — reported as
# "N/N failed" for every scorer, indistinguishable from a spent judge quota.
#
# Under docker compose none of this applies: docker-compose.yml sets these on
# the api service only, and the container never sees an eval run.

# ---- Telemetry: traces, metrics and logs ----------------------------------
# ONE variable configures all three signals. Use the general form, not
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_TRACES_ENDPOINT: each exporter reads its own variables,
# and the metric and log exporters never look at the traces one — they would
# fall back to localhost:4317, which inside the api container is the container
# itself. Traces would arrive and metrics and logs would vanish silently.
#
# gRPC, hence 4317. For HTTP use 4318 AND the protocol line below; a gRPC
# exporter pointed at 4318 fails at export time, not at startup.
OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:4317
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_PROTOCOL=http/protobuf
OTEL_SERVICE_NAME=enterprise-rag-api

# How often metrics are pushed. The SDK default is 60s, which makes a local
# change-and-look loop tedious.
OTEL_METRIC_EXPORT_INTERVAL=15000

# Unset or blank turns tracing off entirely and the service runs unchanged —
# api/observability.py becomes a no-op. Tracing is never a reason it fails.
